1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:26,000
SPEAKERA: Aristotle even reported a size for the Earth: four hundred thousand stadia.

2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:56,000
SPEAKERB: Eratosthenes found a way to actually measure it.

3
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:26,000
SPEAKERA: Far up the Nile, on Egypt's southern frontier, lay the town of Syene. Today it's Aswan.

4
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:56,000
SPEAKERB: And Syene was known for something that happened there once a year.

5
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:26,000
SPEAKERA: At noon on the summer solstice, the longest day of the year, upright sticks there cast no shadow.

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:56,000
SPEAKERB: None at all?

7
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:26,000
SPEAKERA: None. Later writers also tell of a well there, where the noon sunlight reached all the way down to the water.

8
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:56,000
SPEAKERB: Because the Sun was standing straight overhead.

9
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:26,000
SPEAKERA: Syene was taken to lie on the Tropic of Cancer, the furthest north the Sun can ever be overhead.

10
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:56,000
SPEAKERB: But at Alexandria, on the coast, about 5,000 stadia further north, sticks still cast shadows at that noon.

11
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:26,000
SPEAKERA: And that difference is the whole clue.

12
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:56,000
SPEAKERA: If the Earth were flat, and the Sun far away, sticks in both places would cast the same shadow.

13
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:26,000
SPEAKERB: They don't. So the ground between them has to curve.

14
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:56,000
SPEAKERA: And how much it curves over that distance tells you the size of the whole Earth.

15
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:26,000
SPEAKERB: So he needs two numbers: how different the shadows are, and how far apart the cities are.

16
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:56,000
SPEAKERB: So how big was the shadow at Alexandria?

17
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:26,000
SPEAKERA: According to Cleomedes, it was read on a scaphe: a sundial shaped like a bowl.

18
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:56,000
SPEAKERB: A bowl, not just a stick in the ground?

19
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:26,000
SPEAKERA: A bowl. A pointer stands at the bottom, and its tip sits right at the centre of the bowl's curve.

20
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:56,000
SPEAKERB: So at noon, the tip's shadow falls on the inside of the bowl.
